        "employment_record": {
          "value": "Purdue University extension agent for Putnam County (1974-1983); owner of Baird Family Farms, Triple Tree Enterprises, Inc. (gas station operator in Crawfordsville), and Indiana Home Care Plus of Greencastle (home health agency); animal nutritionist at Landmark Cooperative; director of sales and nutrition at Agmax; Putnam County commissioner (2006-2010)",
          "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Baird_(politician)",
          "snippet": "From 1974 to 1983, Baird served as a Purdue University extension agent for Putnam County. [ 15 ] Baird is the owner of Baird Family Farms, Triple Tree Enterprises, Inc. (a gas station operator in Crawfordsville ), and Indiana Home Care Plus of Greencastle, a home health agency. He previously worked as an animal nutritionist at Landmark Cooperative, a feed manufacturer, and as director of sales and nutrition at Agmax. Baird ran for Putnam County commissioner in 2006 and defeated the incumbent, Dennis O'Hair, in the primary. [ 16 ] He represented Marion Township , Greencastle Township , Madison Township , and Clinton Township . [ 17 ] He served as commissioner for the second district until his election to the State House in 2010.",
          "source_type": "llm_extracted_wikipedia"
        }
      },
